# Test: MonadResult.bind — bind an Ok value through a transformation.
# MonadResult is defined in prelude.llt as an instance of the Monad typeclass
# (its bind method delegates to the `and-then` function).
# The type checker does not know about MonadResult (no prelude type env seeding),
# so it warns "undefined variable: MonadResult", but the evaluator succeeds.
[MonadResult.bind [Ok 1] [fn [x] [Ok [+ x 1]]]]
=== error
[E002] undefined variable: MonadResult (defined at 5:2-5:13) (accessed at 5:1-5:48)
  in accessing .bind at 5:2-5:18
  in [<dot-access> ...] at 5:1-5:48
